{
 "metric": "AN-05: strong = share of pixels whose largest RGB channel differs by more than 64 after a 3x3 box blur; mean = mean largest RGB channel difference (0-255); heightDifference = |native - Cordova| px after the points a block ends under the tab bar. Each case passes within its value plus `margin`.",
 "margin": {
  "strong": 0.0015,
  "mean": 0.3,
  "heightDifference": 0
 },
 "reasons": {
  "measurement": "Each case's `measured` is the local run (Xcode 27.2, iOS 26.5 simulator twios_cap_16) of MatrixScreenshotTests after the fixes below; the tolerance is it times 1.5 plus 0.0005 (strong) and times 1.2 plus 0.2 (mean), rounded up, as start-tolerances.json records its headroom for CI's Xcode 26.6.",
  "glyph rasterization": "Most cases: text and glyph edges a pixel apart from WebKit's (its subpixel glyph positions and 1/64 pt layout), every box at the captured position; the same residuals as the 393x852 sets' tolerances.",
  "detail tables and info rows (forecast -3/-4, air -1/-5)": "Up to strong 0.026 and mean 4.0 (air info rows at 375x667, scale 2): left-aligned table text a pixel from the capture, as forecast-tolerances.json's reason for its tables, and at scale 2 each such pixel is a larger share of the block. Inspected side by side: no missing or moved row.",
  "header bar at 375x667 (shell-header)": "Strong 0.0136: the title's glyphs one device pixel apart at scale 2; the bar's height (44 pt, no safe-area inset on the SE) and buttons match.",
  "heightDifference 1": "WebKit rounds each block's pixel edges from 1/64 pt layout; the native block ends on the next pixel.",
  "masked": "The tab bar's home indicator (system UI over the WebView's bottom inset in some captures) and the header bar's page buttons (as ShellScreenshotTests).",
  "fixed before measuring": "The English three-day details (S04) ran their labels into the next day (DayCells now widens a day to its widest line, as WebKit's table); the header block's safe area was 5 pt at every size (now the display's: 0 on the SE, 8 on the Pro Max); the menu's privacy rows were above Send feedback, not after About as the Cordova 1.1.3 build (#2990)."
 },
